    "q-348615": {
      "dom_id": "step-q348615",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{5-3x}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5-3x}{{x}^{2}+2x+1}=\\frac{5-3x}{(x+1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5-3x}{(x+1)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{(x+1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x+1)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n5-3x=A(x+1)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-3(-1) & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ B & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-3(0) & =A(0+1)+8 \\\\ 5 & =A+8 \\\\ A & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5-3x}{(x+1)^{2}}=-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{8}{(x+1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{5-3x}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-2}(-\\frac{3}{x+1}+\\frac{8}{(x+1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x+8{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{-3}^{-2}-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,{|}_{-3}^{-2} \\\\  & =-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-8(-1-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-8(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
