    "q-348616": {
      "dom_id": "step-q348616",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-4x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first factor the denominator of the integrand:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}-4x+4}=\\frac{2x-1}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe must convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-1}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x-2}+\\frac{B}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n2x-1=A(x-2)+B.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2)-1 & =A(2-2)+B \\\\ B & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, plugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-1 & =A(0-2)+3 \\\\ -1 & =-2A+3 \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integrand as the partial sum:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2x-1}{(x-2)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{x-2}+\\frac{3}{(x-2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{2x-1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(\\frac{2}{x-2}+\\frac{3}{(x-2)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{3}^{4}\\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|\\,{|}_{3}^{4}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x-2}\\,{|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)-3(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{1})-3(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
